## 31 recorded 30: fact Rpc method=session/update
item message:2 message open at=3224 text=" times every night. His boots made no sound against the metal; after thirty years on the ragged spit called Crow’s Tooth"
## 33 recorded 32: fact Rpc method=session/update
append message:2 ", he moved with the hush of an owl.\n\nAt the summit, inside the lantern room, the world opened into"
## 35 recorded 34: fact Rpc method=session/update
append message:2 " blackness and salt spray. The wind shrieked against the curved storm panes, rattling the bronze frames with the frantic energy of"
## 37 recorded 36: fact Rpc method=session/update
append message:2 " something desperate to get inside. Arthur paid it no heed. He struck a match—shielding the fragile spark with cu"
## 39 recorded 38: fact Rpc method=session/update
append message:2 "pped, calloused hands—and touched it to the brass burner.\n\nLight bloomed. The great Fresnel lens,"
## 41 recorded 40: fact Rpc method=session/update
append message:2 " taller than a man and carved with concentric rings of heavy French glass, caught the flame and magnified it tenfold, a hundredfold,"
## 43 recorded 42: fact Rpc method=session/update
append message:2 " until a blade of pure, sharp amber thrust outward into the boiling dark.\n\nArthur checked the clockwork weights that kept"
## 45 recorded 44: fact Rpc method=session/update
append message:2 " the lens turning. They were descending smoothly through the center column of the tower. Satisfied, he stepped onto the narrow catwalk"
## 47 recorded 46: fact Rpc method=session/update
append message:2 " that ringed the lantern room, leaning his elbows against the iron railing.\n\nBelow, the Atlantic was a fury of black slate"
## 49 recorded 48: fact Rpc method=session/update
append message:2 " and froth. Out there, invisible beyond the spray, ships were running blind, tossed like woodchips across shoals that"
## 51 recorded 50: fact Rpc method=session/update
append message:2 " could tear an oak keel to kindling. To those men, Arthur was not a person; he was an eye."
## 53 recorded 52: fact Rpc method=session/update
append message:2 " He was a promise that the earth still existed, fixed and unyielding.\n\nHe reached into his woolen coat and pulled out a small, pocket"
## 55 recorded 54: fact Rpc method=session/update
append message:2 "-worn notebook. He recorded the hour, the barometric pressure, the gale force, and the rotation rate of the lens. Routine"
## 57 recorded 56: fact Rpc method=session/update
append message:2 " was the anchor that kept a keeper from drifting away into the solitude. People in town often asked him if he grew lonely"
## 59 recorded 58: fact Rpc method=session/update
append message:2 " out here, six miles from the mainland, with only screaming gulls and the thrum of the foghorn for company.\n\nHe never"
## 61 recorded 60: fact Rpc method=session/update
append message:2 " knew how to explain that solitude here felt vast, not empty. Out on the rock, stripped of human gossip and trivial"
## 63 recorded 62: fact Rpc method=session/update
append message:2 " noise, life was reduced to the clean, elemental terms of darkness and light, danger and salvation.\n\nSuddenly, through"
## 65 recorded 64: fact Rpc method=session/update
append message:2 " the sweep of the beacon, he caught a flash of white canvas—a schooner, dangerously close to the sunken reefs"
## 67 recorded 66: fact Rpc method=session/update
append message:2 " of the outer shoals. Arthur’s heart seized. He watched the beam swing across the dark water, illuminating the vessel just"
## 69 recorded 68: fact Rpc method=session/update
append message:2 " long enough to reveal its listing mast and the panic on its deck.\n\n*Turn,* Arthur willed across the gale"
## 71 recorded 70: fact Rpc method=session/update
append message:2 ", gripping the railing until his knuckles went pale. *See the light. Bear north.*\n\nThe beacon swung around again. The vessel"
## 73 recorded 72: fact Rpc method=session/update
append message:2 " had caught the signal. Its helm responded, carving hard against the white foam, skirting the black teeth of the reef by"
## 75 recorded 74: fact Rpc method=session/update
append message:2 " mere yards before slipping into the safety of deep water.\n\nArthur let out a breath he had not realized he was holding. He"
## 77 recorded 76: fact Rpc method=session/update
append message:2 " wiped salt brine from his beard, adjusted the wick, and began his long descent down the seventy-four steps to wait for dawn."
## 79 recorded 78: fact Rpc method=session/update
